   "anchor": "gfxFontEntry::AutoHBFace (conversion operator); gfxFontEntry (class, new ShouldPublishCharacterMap declaration)",
   "notes": "Primary feature hb-face-lifetime: the conversion operator is ref-qualified (const&, and const&& deleted), so binding the result of GetHBFace() to a raw pointer becomes a compile error. This fixes a dangling pointer in the stealth GetDesignFont (gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp), not a Firefox upstream problem; the comment reports crashes before the fix. Also adds the ShouldPublishCharacterMap declaration (feature font-cmap-publish). The change alters the type of a Mozilla class, so it is not a hook; keep it inline or upstream the fix. Verifier: the dangling-pointer fix is confirmed in the tree (gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp:791 uses const auto face(...)); every other GetHBFace() caller found in gfx/ binds an lvalue (gfxFont.cpp:1394,2810,2849,5197; gfxFontEntry.cpp:257,795,852,927; gfxHarfBuzzShaper.cpp:1373; FontPaletteCache.cpp:25), so the deleted const&& conversion does not break them.",
   "verifier": {
    "changed": [
     "notes"
    ],
    "why": "Checked callers of GetHBFace in gfx/ against the new ref-qualified conversion."
   }
  },
